      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Gothic‑style Grace Evangelical Church, built in 1902, is a National Register landmark still used by the local Methodist congregation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historylink.org/File/23303",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Little Falls Fire Clay Factory, the county’s largest in the early 1900s, employed about 75 men making bricks, tiles, and pipes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historylink.org/File/23303",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 2015 land purchase doubled Vader’s park area, funded by a $10,000 grant, expanding green space for residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
